 in the CI docs-gates action (.github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml)'. The Verification already runs those two scripts directly, which is the correct gate; keep '`make lint` passes' only for the ruff/lint concerns it actually covers.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving command that asserts §I1 no longer reads 'follow-up' and now reads 'implemented' (e.g. `grep -n 'implemented' near §I1 and confirm the prior 'follow-up' note is gone), not just that '0106' appears.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: \"docs/concurrency.md §I1 is promoted from 'follow-up' to implemented and cross-references ADR 0106\"","Verify only greps for the literal '0106', taxonomy item (6): prose-vs-assertion target — the status transition is not asserted"],"finding":"The concurrency.md promotion criterion ('promoted from follow-up to implemented and cross-references ADR 0106') is only verified by `grep -n '0106' docs/concurrency.md`, which proves the cross-reference string is present but does NOT prove the §I1 status text was actually changed from 'follow-up' to 'implemented'. The promotion half of the claim is unmeasured.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb3ce58e28f6a11a3","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification: `grep -n '0106' docs/concurrency.md docs/adr/README.md`","norm_id":"n5576948a4652160e","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The ADR reference is added but the 'follow-up' wording is left in place; grep still passes green while the promotion never happened."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add: `grep -nA3 '§I1' docs/concurrency.md | grep -iq implemented` and a negative check that the old 'follow-up' phrasing for §I1 is removed.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Have the ADR record the rationale for the 30d default (relationship to stale-clone override window and expected reconnect cadence) rather than asserting it bare.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope: 'the horizon config key (default 30d, portable ...)'","T2 STEP-1 signal: a default/threshold asserted rather than derived"],"finding":"The 30d horizon default is asserted without a stated rationale or derivation. It is configurable (mitigating changeability), but the ADR is the natural place to record WHY 30d and how an operator should reason about changing it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1dc908aae5f1d363","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / AC: 'the N-day horizon as a portable config key (default 30d)'","norm_id":"nc96cfd24cf7b87eb","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Future maintainers debate whether 30d is safe for clone-drift without any recorded reasoning tie to stale-clone override behavior."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the ADR must DECIDE between authorship_ledger carriage and enforce_since re-anchor (and on what criterion), or may present both — so the executor is not left to pick silently.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.468,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope: 'SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage OR enforce_since re-anchor for signature/authorship verifiability'","Signal (6)/placeholder: the OR presents two designs without ranking or a decision rule"],"finding":"The signature/authorship-verifiability requirement is stated as a disjunction ('SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage OR enforce_since re-anchor') and the plan leaves the choice of which mechanism the ADR must adopt to the executor. For an ADR — whose purpose is to record a decision — the acceptable answer set is clear, but which one is chosen is a real design decision deferred.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5118678d03a59492","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / AC: 'SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage OR enforce_since re-anchor'","norm_id":"n1e56931193dd8e54","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor authors the ADR picking whichever mechanism is easier, potentially not the one the epic intends."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a prior-art subsection to ADR 0106 that (a) surveys how peer git-native trackers (git-bug, git-appraise, jujutsu) and general distributed VCS handle below-horizon history reclamation / GC and stale-clone reconvergence after a rewrite, and (b) justifies WHY the FORCED destructive remote-override is chosen over the non-destructive union-recovery / gc-reachability posture that docs/concurrency.md §sync already adopts from those same peers.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope: 'a clone whose last convergence is older than N days overrides local with remote rather than reintroducing pre-collapse history by rebase' + accepted residual 'a >N-day-drifted clone's divergent local work is discarded'.","docs/concurrency.md §sync (line ~745): 'The fix follows the universal peer pattern (git-bug, git-appraise, jujutsu): make recovery **non-destructive** so the reflog is never load-bearing.' and the 'gc-reachability == recovery guarantee' co-design — cited for the non-destructive property this ADR's forced-override reverses.","docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md G3: git-bug 'packs ops into fewer objects with a documented cache' and Fossil sidesteps small-object blowup — directly relevant prior art for the object-growth problem the collapse lever targets, unconsidered.","Web search confirms distributed history rewrite is a recognized problem: 'The repository is not the only copy; every clone holds the old history and will happily merge it back in' (git-automation.com history-rewriting-and-recovery)."],"finding":"The ADR proposes a novel distributed-history-rewrite pattern (below-horizon commit/tree collapse of a multi-clone append-only store) plus a FORCED stale-clone remote-override that discards divergent local work, but the plan requires no consideration of how peer git-native trackers handle below-horizon history reclamation / stale-clone reconvergence — even though rebar's own docs/concurrency.md (the document this ADR promotes and cross-references) already cites those peers (git-bug, git-appraise, jujutsu 'gc-reachability == recovery guarantee') for the exact OPPOSITE, NON-DESTRUCTIVE reconvergence posture the forced-override inverts.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff5743bcff887058e","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope paragraph ('stale-clone detection + FORCED remote-override protocol') and Acceptance Criteria (the only justification demanded is 'a proof that invariants I1-I9 still hold').","norm_id":"n9837e20e551b0efb","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer asks why rebar's below-horizon reclamation discards drifted local work rather than following the same non-destructive peer pattern the sync section commits to — the ADR offers only an I1-I9 proof, not a prior-art comparison, so the novelty vs the established peer approach is unjustified."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity